## 1. Definitions

**"Licensor"** means the copyright holder named in the copyright notice accompanying the Licensed Materials.

**"Licensed Materials"** means the original source code, website design as expressed in that code, layouts, components, styles, scripts, configuration, build tooling, and documentation distributed with this License, in any form. This includes source form, compiled, bundled, minified, or otherwise built output, and the code as served to visitors of a deployed website. It excludes Third-Party Materials and Recipient Content.

**"Third-Party Materials"** means software, libraries, fonts, icons, images, media, trademarks, and other material owned by someone other than the Licensor and licensed separately.

**"Recipient Content"** means text, photographs, video, logos, names, data, and other material supplied by or belonging to an Authorized Recipient. This includes every image or likeness of an identifiable person.

**"Authorized Recipient"** means a person or organization for whom the Licensor has created or supplied a particular website or project and whom the Licensor has named as an Authorized Recipient in writing.

**"Project"** means the particular website or project for which an Authorized Recipient was supplied the Licensed Materials.

**"Authorized Agent"** means an employee, volunteer, member, or hosting provider acting on behalf of an Authorized Recipient, solely for that Recipient's purposes.

**"Necessary Maintenance"** means a change to the Licensed Materials that is strictly required to keep the Project functioning as supplied. It is limited to:

- repairing breakage;
- applying security fixes;
- updating dependencies where required for security or continued operation; and
- adapting to changes in hosting, platforms, or external services.

It does not include new features, redesigns, visual or layout changes, restructuring, or any other improvement.

**"Distribute"** means to give, transfer, publish, or make available a copy of the Licensed Materials, or any part or modified version of them, to any other person, other than through a Public Deployment.

**"Public Deployment"** means making the Licensed Materials, or any website or software built from them, accessible over a network to anyone other than you and, if you are an Authorized Recipient, your Authorized Agents.

**"Non-Production Use"** means running the Licensed Materials only on your own devices or in an environment accessible only to you, for learning, evaluation, or testing, and not for any operational, business, organizational, or internal production purpose. An internal or intranet website is not Non-Production Use.

**"Template Use"** means using the Licensed Materials, any part of them, or any version derived from them as a template, theme, starter, framework, component library, or basis for any website, application, or product other than the Project.

**"You"** means the person or organization exercising rights under this License.

## 2. Source Availability

The Licensor may make the Licensed Materials publicly available for inspection, education, security review, archival, and evaluation. Making them publicly available does not place them in the public domain and grants no rights except those in this License.

Anyone may:

a. view, read, and study the Licensed Materials;

b. download or clone them, and fork them within a hosting platform where that platform's terms permit forking, for personal archival, research, educational, or evaluation purposes only; and

c. run and modify them for Non-Production Use.

No other right is granted. A fork, clone, or download is a copy held only for the purposes above. It gives no right to Distribute, to make a Public Deployment, or to engage in Template Use.

