## 5. Revocation and Termination

a. **Revocation.** The Licensor may revoke an Authorized Recipient's license at any time by written notice. Revocation takes effect on the date stated in the notice, or immediately if no date is stated.

b. **Termination for breach.** All rights granted to you under this License terminate automatically if you breach any of its conditions. If you cure the breach within 30 days after becoming aware of it, the Licensor may, at its discretion, reinstate your rights in writing.

c. **Effect.** When your rights end, you must stop all use and Public Deployment of the Licensed Materials and delete all copies in your possession or control, except copies you are required by law to keep.

d. **Survival.** Sections 1, 3, 4.5, 5(c), 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, and 12 survive revocation or termination.

